From 8c12737d1dc20ef1bffc3cc91df42677a3317efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CEC: take no input of the TV through an adapter of another
 output

An HDMI or DisplayPort output that carries only the sound has a CEC
adapter of its own: an AV receiver on the HDMI port of the board, a DP
to HDMI converter whose CEC the kernel tunnels over DP-AUX, while the
picture goes to the TV from another graphics card. Through it Kodi made
itself the active source and woke the TV at its start, at the start of
each video and when the screensaver ended, as "Switch source to this
device on startup" and "Devices to power on during startup" say: the
receiver switched to the PC and the TV switched to the receiver's input,
away from Kodi's picture (issue #24, a Pioneer on DP-1 of i915, an LG B7
on an RTX 3050).

The kernel says which DRM connector a CEC adapter is of
(CEC_ADAP_G_CONNECTOR_INFO: the number of the card and the id of the
connector), and the windowing system now says which output carries the
picture (UTILS::CDrivenOutput, beside CDrivenDisplay: the node of its
card and the id of its connector). Through an adapter of another output
(PeripheralCecPicture.h):
- libCEC is configured without the activation of the source and
  without the TV among the devices to wake, whatever the settings say;
  the settings keep what the user chose;
- Kodi's own requests to make it the active source are not sent;
- with libcec-9015 of LibreELEC Hades, a routing change to it does not
  take the TV's input either.
The keys of the remote, the volume of an amplifier, the standby commands
and the answers to what the TV itself asks are as before. An adapter
that is on the picture's output, or one whose output is not known (a
Pulse-Eight on USB, CEC that the kernel ties to no connector, a kernel
that does not say, the picture's output not known yet), is as before.
When Kodi's picture moves to another output, the adapter is judged again
and libCEC configured again, as for a change of its settings. The log
says, at INFO and once for each change, which it is and why.

Tests: TestPeripheralCecPicture (the outputs of #24), 5 pass; four
mutants are caught.
